{title: Fairest Lord Jesus}
{artist: Munster Gesangbuch (1677); anon. tr. c. 1850 / Joseph A. Seiss (1823-1904)}
{key: Eb}
{copyright: Public Domain}

{sov: Verse 1}
[Eb]Fairest Lord Jesus, [Ab]Ruler of [Bb]all na[Eb]ture,
[Eb]O Thou of [Cm]God and [Fm]man the [Bb]Son,
[Ab]Thee will I [Eb]cherish, [Bb]Thee will I [Cm]honor,
[Eb]Thou, my soul’s [Ab]glory, [Bb]joy, and [Eb]crown.
{eov}

{sov: Verse 2}
[Eb]Fair are the meadows, [Ab]fairer still [Bb]the wood[Eb]lands,
[Eb]Robed in the [Cm]blooming [Fm]garb of [Bb]spring;
[Ab]Jesus is [Eb]fairer, [Bb]Jesus is [Cm]purer,
[Eb]Who makes the [Ab]woeful [Bb]heart to [Eb]sing.
{eov}

{sov: Verse 3}
[Eb]Fair is the sunshine, [Ab]fairer still [Bb]the moon[Eb]light,
[Eb]And all the [Cm]twinkling [Fm]starry [Bb]host;
[Ab]Jesus shines [Eb]brighter, [Bb]Jesus shines [Cm]purer
[Eb]Than all the [Ab]angels [Bb]heaven can [Eb]boast.
{eov}

{sov: Verse 4}
[Eb]Beautiful Savior! [Ab]Lord of [Bb]all the na[Eb]tions!
[Eb]Son of [Cm]God and [Fm]Son of [Bb]Man!
[Ab]Glory and [Eb]honor, [Bb]praise, ado[Cm]ration,
[Eb]Now and for[Ab]ever[Bb]more be [Eb]Thine.
{eov}
